# Build 95a: SHU raises the defense of the member chosen, not the
# first member's.
#
# TechAction_Shu (ps2.asm:3288) sets d4 to 0 and joins TechAction_Sashu's
# loop at loc_22FA with a5 still on the command's target word -- the
# member the cursor picked -- where Sashu, Saner and Deban point a5 at
# party_member_id first. Ner (loc_235C) is the same. Up to build 95 the
# port's Shu and Ner took party_member_id[0] whoever was chosen, so
# Rolf's defense rose from 133 to 153 here and Nei's stayed at 64.
#
# Party 4 30 is Rolf, Nei, Rudo, Amy; Amy knows SHU (her second battle
# technique). The party triangle's stops run in the screen's order
# (Battle_CharacterIdIndex): stop 2 is Nei, party position 1.

start battle 213
party 4 30
wait idle
expect stat 0 defense 133
expect stat 1 defense 64
press down                   # STGY
press c
wait idle
press c                      # ORDR
wait idle
press right
wait ticks 3
press right
wait ticks 3
press right                  # Amy
wait ticks 3
press c
wait idle
press right                  # TECH
wait ticks 3
press c
wait idle
expect menu $66 1            # RES SHU DEBAN FOI, the lamp on RES
press down                   # SHU
wait ticks 3
expect menu $66 2
press c
wait idle
expect menu $00 0            # the party triangle
press right
wait ticks 3
press right
wait ticks 3
expect menu $00 2            # on Nei
press c
wait idle
expect menu $60              # back to FIGHT / STGY
press c                      # FIGHT
wait script $120D            # "Defense ability increases!"
wait ticks 60
shot 01_defense_up
expect command tech
expect stat 1 defense 84     # Nei's, up by 20
expect stat 0 defense 133    # Rolf's as it was
